                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "I\u2019d prefer you don\u2019t do this. Once C++26 is implemented we will likely migrate off stdexec (since it is a reference implementation). The reason for the sdbusplus/async.hpp is as an abstraction."
                },
                {
                    "file": "requester/handler.hpp",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Aditya Kurdunkar",
                        "email": "adityakurdunkar2@gmail.com",
                        "username": "akurdunkar"
                    },
                    "message": "Most of the pldm code uses primitives from `exec` directly. So should they be moved to sdbusplus/async? For e.g `exec::task` -> `sdbusplus::async::task`"
                },
                {
                    "file": "requester/handler.hpp",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Aditya Kurdunkar",
                        "email": "adityakurdunkar2@gmail.com",
                        "username": "akurdunkar"
                    },
                    "message": "Done."
                },
